.nh
.TH "RAIL0" "1" "Aug 2026" "rail0 CLI" ""

.SH NAME
rail0-auth-revoke-all - End EVERY session of an address, on every machine (for a key you no longer trust)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrail0 auth revoke-all [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke every session the gateway has issued to an address — the ones on this
machine, on other machines, and any a thief is holding.

.PP
\&'auth logout' cannot do this: it revokes ONE token, the one stored here. This is
per ADDRESS. The gateway records a cutoff instant, and every session of the
address issued before it is refused from then on, including this machine's.

.PP
It is authorized by a fresh signature of the address's KEY, not by the session:
whoever reacts to a leaked key holds the wallet, not the stolen token. The signed
message says "Sign out of RAIL0 everywhere", so a login signature cannot be
replayed to trigger it. The key is resolved like every signing command (-p as
0x hex, @name for a keychain key, or RAIL0_PRIVATE_KEY).

.PP
Afterwards, sign in again with 'rail0 auth login'. If you suspect the key itself
leaked, this ends the sessions but does not make the key safe: move the funds
and stop using it.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for revoke-all

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--private-key\fP=""
	Key OF the address whose sessions to end: 0x hex, @name for an OS-keychain key, or RAIL0_PRIVATE_KEY

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	Skip the confirmation prompt (required to run non-interactively)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--agent\fP[=false]
	Agent mode: one JSON envelope on stdout, JSON events on stderr, no prompts (env: RAIL0_AGENT=1)

.PP
\fB--base-url\fP=""
	RAIL0 gateway base URL (env: RAIL0_BASE_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Print HTTP request/response details to stderr

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Force plain (uncolored) JSON output (useful in scripts)

.PP
\fB--pretty\fP[=false]
	Use the key-value/table view instead of JSON (terminal only)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Print only the result's id/hash, one per line (useful in scripts)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  rail0 auth revoke-all -p @merchant-key
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBrail0-auth(1)\fP
